WEBVTT

00:00:00.372 --> 00:00:09.524
TV screens put a store’s live orders, today’s tasks, and who’s on duty on any TV. In this video, you’ll set up a screen and connect a TV.

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:19.668
Here’s the front counter TV. Open orders sit in three columns, longest wait on top, and anything waiting fifteen minutes or more turns red.

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:27.945
In the kitchen, the TV shows today’s tasks and checklists, one column per person, marked done, now, or overdue.

00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:40.627
To set one up, open Order Tracking or Operations with a store chosen, and click Show on TV. Name the screen, and tick what it should show. With more than one view, the TV takes turns.

00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:53.133
On the TV, open its web browser at your workspace address, followed by slash TV. It shows a six-letter code: type it here, and the TV switches to your screen in a few seconds.

00:00:54.157 --> 00:01:02.456
A screen is read-only and needs no sign-in. Managers see every screen in Screens and devices, and can turn one off at any time.
